<title>SPAIN: Spain Cantabrico '96 net profit up 27.4 pct.</title>
<headline>Spain Cantabrico '96 net profit up 27.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full 1996 results for Hidrocantabrico in billions of pesetas, according to documents obtained by Reuters:</p>
<p> Income				   105.40    vs    113.33</p>
<p> Gross operating profit		45.23    vs     41.53</p>
<p> Ordinary profit			 22.64    vs     17.65</p>
<p> Net profit				16.49    vs     12.94</p>
<p> Consumption			     42.10    vs     54.30</p>
<p> Operating costs			 18.07    vs     17.51</p>
<p> Depreciation			    14.36    vs     13.89</p>
<p> Net financial expenses		 8.85    vs     10.25</p>
<p> Provisions			     (0.029)   vs	0.31</p>
<p> Capitalised expenses		  (0.58)   vs     (0.57)</p>
<p> Extraordinary profit		  (1.44)   vs	0.96</p>
<p> Pretax profit			   21.20    vs     18.61</p>
<p>NOTE: Full name Hidroelectrica del Cantabrico. Figures are consolidated.</p>
<p>The firm said it would pay a fourth and final dividend on March 15, bringing the total dividend to 200 pesetas per share, to be approved by shareholder</p>
</text>
